                        "form": "bumbershoots"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7de4ace4-f4ed-3498-b495-408199115c4f",
                        "entry_id": "ae8c5cac-9b11-309c-b5f9-49002b877edd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An umbrella."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "humorous",
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ed002c43-3129-4bb4-8f30-f44a8f256b68",
                                "sense_id": "7de4ace4-f4ed-3498-b495-408199115c4f",
                                "text": "It smells like rain. Perhaps we should take along a bumbershoot."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "906b4732-39bc-4e7e-aaf4-51e7162840f9",
                                "sense_id": "7de4ace4-f4ed-3498-b495-408199115c4f",
                                "text": "Oh! Hang the bumbershoot! [Flings umbrella away, clasps Mrs. Dobbs wildly.]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fb39d244-3cca-4c49-90f1-d5e7802cda50",
                                "sense_id": "7de4ace4-f4ed-3498-b495-408199115c4f",
                                "text": "Little drops of water / It is safe to bet / If you have no bumbershoot, / Make you doosid wet."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a5f3871a-9fe0-4458-b1d5-e9c2822400ea",
                                "sense_id": "7de4ace4-f4ed-3498-b495-408199115c4f",
                                "text": "\"It—it belongs in our family,\" said Button-Bright, beginning to eat and speaking between bites. \"This umbrella has been in our family years, an' years, an' years. But it was tucked away up in our attic an' no one ever used it 'cause it wasn't pretty.\" / \"Don't blame 'em much,\" remarked Cap'n Bill, gazing at it curiously; \"it's a pretty old-lookin' bumbershoot.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "09bb9996-ee37-47e7-8072-6f83a828cf44",
                                "sense_id": "7de4ace4-f4ed-3498-b495-408199115c4f",
                                "text": "Two women pickets, Krkossa and Menefee, walked the picket line in front of the Respondent's studio for 1½ hours on 1 day carrying large old-fashioned men's umbrella (perhaps better described by the word \"bumbershoots\") thereby, according to the Respondent's theory, committing serious strike misconduct by interfering with pedestrian traffic in front of the Respondent's studio, by preventing others on the street or sidewalk from reading advertising material painted on the approximately 50-foot expanse of windows of the Respondent's building facing upon the street, and by reason of the hazard allegedly created of physical damage to passing pedestrians from the ribs of said bumbershoots."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "563f7985-d912-4812-bcd7-b32d1bc22b26",
                                "sense_id": "7de4ace4-f4ed-3498-b495-408199115c4f",
                                "text": "Nick Fury. Hey, Percy! Get that blasted umbrella outta my ribs!! / Percy Pinkerton. I beg your par … Oh! You mean my bumbershoot!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3a06e626-fe6d-4de5-ba81-efdcddc22b8e",
                                "sense_id": "7de4ace4-f4ed-3498-b495-408199115c4f",
                                "text": "Me ol' bamboo, me ol' bamboo / You'd better never bother with me ol' bamboo. / You can have me hat or me bumbershoot / But you'd better never bother with me ol' bamboo."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d105a644-1d88-44ab-b5e9-807c314cb5c8",
                                "sense_id": "7de4ace4-f4ed-3498-b495-408199115c4f",
                                "text": "Wait a minute! Where's my hat? Where— and somebody stole my bumbershoot!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6b26a944-a152-4677-8648-6a74e04f048e",
                                "sense_id": "7de4ace4-f4ed-3498-b495-408199115c4f",
                                "text": "On the march, it began to rain, I had an umbrella, but at 5:51 we copped out for our dinner-date, when just in sight of the sidestreet leading to the U. N., solid with motionless people under their parapluies and bumbershoots; that’s the way it shone back to us, international."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3251aa0a-1891-412d-8d24-d702d3dc6997",
                                "sense_id": "7de4ace4-f4ed-3498-b495-408199115c4f",
                                "text": "Drizzles and mizzles. Recruit a bumbershoot."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "62747742-a87b-4efe-9003-5ac6d51b64b5",
                                "sense_id": "7de4ace4-f4ed-3498-b495-408199115c4f",
                                "text": "She was terrified as a pair of footmen—dressed in full sixteenth-century livery, powdered wigs and all—cut through the chaos and ushered them inside the Waldorf, shielding them from the flying debris with bumbershoots."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
